</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Klein</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Impact on Condom Use of the "100% Jeune" Social Marketing Program in Cameroon</article-title><source>PSI Research Division Working Paper 54</source><year>2003</year></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><source>PSI Youth Sexual Health Programme: Cameroon, Rwanda, Madagascar</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>Washington, D.C.: Population Services International</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ward</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Personal communication. [E-mail]</article-title><year>2003</year></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bandura</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><source>Social Learning Theory</source><year>1977</year><publisher-name>Englewood Cliffs, New Jersey: Prentice-Hall</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Becker</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Health Belief Model and Personal Health Behavior</article-title><source>Health Educ Monogr</source><year>1974</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>236</fpage><lpage>473</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Janz</surname><given-names>NK</given-names></name><name><surname>Becker</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Health Belief Model: A Decade Later</article-title><source>Health Educ Q</source><year>1984</year>